This is the classic "Next Greater Element II" problem. The standard approach is to use a monotonic stack and iterate over the array twice (2n iterations) to handle the circular nature.

Approach:
- Use a stack that stores indices (or values) of elements in decreasing order.
- Iterate i from 0 to 2n-1, using i % n as the actual index.
- For each element nums[i % n], pop elements from the stack while the top has a smaller value; those popped elements have nums[i % n] as their next greater element.
- Push i % n onto the stack (only need to push during first pass, but pushing in second pass is harmless as long as we handle duplicates correctly — actually pushing in second pass is fine too since those indices already have answers or won't be needed).

