Looking at this problem, I need to implement full-string regex matching with `.` (any single char) and `*` (zero or more of preceding element).

**Approach: Dynamic Programming**

Define `dp[i][j]` = true if the first `i` characters of `s` match the first `j` characters of `p`.

**Base cases:**
- `dp[0][0] = true` (empty matches empty)
- `dp[0][j]` for `j > 0`: only true if pattern is like `a*`, `a*b*`, etc. — i.e., `p[j-1] == '*'` and `dp[0][j-2]` is true.

**Transitions:**
- If `p[j-1]` is a letter or `.`: `dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1]` when `s[i-1]` matches `p[j-1]`.
- If `p[j-1]` is `*`:
  - Zero occurrences of the preceding element: `dp[i][j] = dp[i][j-2]`
  - One or more occurrences: if `s[i-1]` matches `p[j-2]`, then `dp[i][j] |= dp[i-1][j]` (consume one char of `s`, keep the `x*` pattern active).

**Verification with examples:**
- `s="aa", p="a"` → `dp[2][1]` requires `dp[1][0]` = false → false ✓
- `s="aa", p="a*"` → `dp[2][2]`: zero-occ gives `dp[2][0]`=false, but consuming one 'a' gives `dp[1][2]`=true → true ✓
- `s="ab", p=".*"` → `.` matches both chars via `.*` repetition → true ✓

Also checked `s="aaa", p="a*a"` → true (the `a*` matches "aa", final `a` matches last char).

The problem guarantees each `*` has a preceding valid character, so accessing `p[j-2]` when `p[j-1]=='*'` is safe (j ≥ 2).

Complexity: O(m·n) time and space, trivial for lengths ≤ 20.

```cpp
#include <string>
#include <vector>
using namespace std;

class Solution {
public:
    bool isMatch(string s, string p) {
        int m = s.size(), n = p.size();
        vector<vector<bool>> dp(m + 1, vector<bool>(n + 1, false));
        dp[0][0] = true;

        // Patterns like a*, a*b*, ... can match the empty string
        for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {
            if (p[j - 1] == '*') {
                dp[0][j] = dp[0][j - 2];
            }
        }

        for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {
                if (p[j - 1] == '*') {
                    // zero occurrences of the preceding element
                    dp[i][j] = dp[i][j - 2];
                    // one or more occurrences
                    if (s[i - 1] == p[j - 2] || p[j - 2] == '.') {
                        dp[i][j] = dp[i][j] || dp[i - 1][j];
                    }
                } else if (s[i - 1] == p[j - 1] || p[j - 1] == '.') {
                    dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j - 1];
                }
            }
        }

        return dp[m][n];
    }
};
```

