2. At each level, check if any string in the queue is valid. If yes, collect all valid strings at this level and stop.
3. Otherwise, generate all strings by removing one parenthesis character (only '(' or ')'), dedupe using a set, and add to next level.

Alternative: DFS approach that's more efficient. Compute the minimum number of removals needed:
