The problem: shift 2D grid k times. Treat grid as flattened 1D array of size m*n. Shifting once moves each element to the next position (circular). So after k shifts, element at flat index i moves to index (i + k) % (m*n).

So result[(i + k) % total] = grid[i / n][i % n], or equivalently result[i / n][i % n] = grid[((i - k) mod total) / n][...].

