1. **Each node has at most one parent** — if any node appears as a child of two different nodes (indegree > 1), it's invalid.
2. **Exactly one root exists** — exactly one node with indegree 0. Zero roots means a cycle covers everything; multiple roots means a forest (disconnected).
3. **All nodes reachable from the root** — BFS/DFS from the root must visit all `n` nodes. This catches cycles not reachable from the root (any cycle reachable from the root would already create an indegree-2 node, caught by check 1).

